  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="season">
    <h2 id="season">When is grass pollen season in Australia?</h2>
    <p>In Melbourne, Sydney, Adelaide, Perth, Canberra and Hobart, grass pollen starts in September, is high in October and peaks in November and December, before tailing off in January. From Brisbane north, the summer grasses keep it going from November to February and into March. Cypress pine (Callitris) comes earlier, in late winter and spring, peaking in September.</p>
    {{ m.heatmapCalendarEn(ROWS, NAMES, us.MONTH_NAMES_EN, INTENSITY_LABELS_EN, build.month) }}
    <p class="fine-print">Respira's seasonal calendar for Australia, by climate zone: an estimate, not a measurement. The line between the two grass rows is 28°S, between the Gold Coast and Brisbane. Seasons shift with rain and with the year's weather; the app shows the level reported for your own location each day.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section flow" aria-labelledby="what">
    <h2 id="what">What Respira shows in Australia</h2>
    <p><strong>Today's level for your city.</strong> Grass and cypress pine, from the Google Pollen API, updated daily for wherever you are. When a species has no reading for your location, the app says so instead of showing a zero.</p>
    <p><strong>The coming days.</strong> A forecast by day, so you can plan the weekend or a run before you go.</p>
    <p><strong>A map of the whole country.</strong> The level in each city at a glance, plus air quality for the same place.</p>
    <p><strong>A symptom diary.</strong> Note how each day went; the app pairs it with the pollen that day.</p>
    <p><strong>Alerts and a PDF report for your GP</strong> are part of Respira Pro: set a level per allergen and get told the morning it is reached.</p>
  </section>

